g care delays. However, AI-driven prior authorization is facing resistance, as it may increase wrongful denials of health insurance coverage. A 2025 American Medical Association survey of physicians revealed significant concern about the application of AI tools , with 61 percent of doctors worrying that AI will exacerbate denials of what they deem are necessary treatments. Read full article Commentsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;0pSCTRuRX05jMoxZma2fjMl9MPVuYBuGlyQQtrRJUusƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx3Will AI fix prior authorizationâ€”or make it worse?ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;AgBExvCFScWYj6u2pBT0nSITn-yfyabh2vSVWZ14GcQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkoSyndicationItemƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;6aOMm-Q4dFc7n5AHq0pG9XgafgiNPYlU0haLmq0EEEYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxThttps://arstechnica.com/ai/2026/07/will-ai-fix-prior-authorization-or-make-it-worse/ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;5boRLjGmPOxa8n82KOUuKSUTNIClOJ6N4GKI0f-OPwEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx0will-ai-fix-prior-authorization-or-make-it-worseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;5fhOcRQse5BwSIrRfYPLPX9nGJEOdSk3HITgIsRkS70ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwSyndicationSourceBundleƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;3EDCWWbdEFnz6u56IY5R1gXmINJ9Qc2PJ2hazAp59Fkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkjtechnologyƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Oq4ss37vu66bkXjy8HbzBQjEnPWSFIyUWdUjT9-GovQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdst